 but inside an uptrend with strength behind it an upthrust is 'in the wrong place', at resistance / new highs (low significance); effort to fall 16 Sep on 1.4x volume, closed on the low - but a wide down bar inside an uptrend: watch whether it is tested (low significance); last 5 bars: down bars on heavier volume (1.8x vs 1.2x) = supply in control; latest 18 Sep: down bar on 2.70x volume, no VSA sign; balance neutral 47/100.","status":"failed","last_sign":{"name":"Effort to fall","d":"2026-09-16","pol":-1,"sig":0.36,"tier":"low","why":"a wide down bar inside an uptrend: watch whether it is tested","ref":null},"key_bars":[{"name":"No supply","d":"2026-08-07","pol":1,"sig":0.72,"tier":"moderate"},{"name":"Test in a rising market","d":"2026-08-12","pol":1,"sig":0.7,"tier":"moderate"},{"name":"Test","d":"2026-08-13","pol":1,"sig":0.9,"tier":"moderate"},{"name":"Effort to fall","d":"2026-09-16","pol":-1,"sig":0.36,"tier":"low"}],"asof":null},"scores":{"overall":31,"group":"SIC 131x (Oil & Gas Extraction)","group_rank":40,"group_n":52,"sector_rank":92,"sector_n":126,"earn":13}},"biz":{"name":"Range Resources Corp","desc":"Range Resources is an exploration and production firm whose operations represent a pure play in the Marcellus shale, located in the Appalachian region of Southwest Pennsylvania. The company went public as Lomak Petroleum in 1980 and later reorganized as Range Resources in 1998. After an expensive 10-year venture with a multibasin strategy, Range Resources found its identity as an Appalachian natural gas producer, offloading its Permian assets in 2013. Range quickly became a leading US gas producer after its merger with Memorial Resource Development in 2016. Following the merger, Range saw its operational unit costs rise to an uncompetitive level and subsequently sold the assets in 2020 to return to its roots as an Appalachian producer.","desc_src":"Massive (formerly Polygon.io) ticker details","sic":"1311","sic_desc":"Crude Petroleum & Natural Gas","sect